        <p>
          Just outside the top 10, Ohio ($77,146) and Arizona
          ($77,074) round out the states where take-home stays above
          $77,000. To run your own numbers for any of these states,
          try the
          <a href="/en-us/states/texas-paycheck-calculator/">Texas
          paycheck calculator</a> or the
          <a href="/en-us/states/florida-paycheck-calculator/">Florida
          paycheck calculator</a> — each state has its own calculator
          with its own 2026 brackets.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="bottom-10" class="article-section">
        <h2>The Bottom 10 States</h2>
        <p>
          At the other end of the ranking, Oregon is last by a wide
          margin: its $8,176 state tax bill is more than $2,000 above
          the next-highest state, Hawaii at $6,157. The rest of the
          bottom 10 cluster between $4,860 and $6,157 of state tax.
        </p>

        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Rank</th>
